  { id: 'p186', group: 'cohesion', en: 'With the growing popularity of ...,', zh: '随着……的日益普及，……', note: '放在首句交代背景，后面必须紧跟主句，不能单独成句；of 是介词，只接名词或 V-ing，不能接句子。', ex: 'With the growing popularity of online classes, students can review lessons anywhere.', exZh: '随着网课日益普及，学生可以在任何地方复习功课。' },
  { id: 'p187', group: 'cohesion', en: 'It is widely acknowledged that ...', zh: '人们普遍认为……', note: '开头用来建立共识，比 I think 更客观；it 是形式主语，that 后必须是一个完整句子且 that 不可省略。', ex: 'It is widely acknowledged that reading shapes the way we think.', exZh: '人们普遍认为阅读塑造我们的思维方式。' },
  { id: 'p188', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Nowadays, ... has become an inseparable part of our lives.', zh: '如今，……已成为我们生活中不可分割的一部分。', note: '科技与网络类话题的万能首句；part 前的冠词 an 最容易漏，写成 become inseparable part 会扣分。', ex: 'Nowadays, the smartphone has become an inseparable part of our lives.', exZh: '如今，智能手机已成为我们生活中不可分割的一部分。' },
  { id: 'p189', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Recently, the issue of ... has drawn widespread attention.', zh: '近来，……的问题引发了广泛关注。', note: '用于引出有争议的社会现象，时态用现在完成时；issue of 后接名词，别接 that 从句。', ex: 'Recently, the issue of food waste has drawn widespread attention.', exZh: '近来，食物浪费问题引发了广泛关注。' },
  { id: 'p190', group: 'cohesion', en: 'When it comes to ..., opinions vary from person to person.', zh: '一提到……，人们的看法各不相同。', note: '从背景过渡到讨论的转场句；it 不可省略，to 是介词，后面只能接名词或 V-ing。', ex: 'When it comes to homework, opinions vary from person to person.', exZh: '一提到作业，人们的看法各不相同。' },
  { id: 'p191', group: 'cohesion', en: 'From my perspective, ...', zh: '在我看来，……', note: '提出个人观点，比 I think 正式；逗号后直接接完整句子，不要再重复 I believe。', ex: 'From my perspective, failure is a lesson rather than a shame.', exZh: '在我看来，失败是一堂课而非耻辱。' },
  { id: 'p192', group: 'cohesion', en: 'As far as I am concerned, ...', zh: '就我而言，……', note: '表明个人立场，常放第二段首句；结尾必须是 concerned，用口语化的 as for me 会拉低语域。', ex: 'As far as I am concerned, the plan is worth trying.', exZh: '在我看来，这个计划值得一试。' },
  { id: 'p193', group: 'cohesion', en: 'I am firmly convinced that ...', zh: '我坚定地认为……', note: '结尾段重申立场时用它，语气比 I believe 更有力；主语一致时用 am，别写成 I am convince。', ex: 'I am firmly convinced that effort matters more than luck.', exZh: '我坚信努力比运气更重要。' },
  { id: 'p194', group: 'cohesion', en: 'My own view on the matter is that ...', zh: '我对这件事的看法是……', note: '书信、倡议书里表明立场很自然；is 后的 that 引导表语从句，省略 that 容易被判结构不完整。', ex: 'My own view on the matter is that honesty comes first.', exZh: '我对这件事的看法是诚实至上。' },
  { id: 'p195', group: 'cohesion', en: 'First and foremost, ...', zh: '首先也是最重要的一点，……', note: '引出第一条理由，比 firstly 更有分量；逗号后必须是完整句子，不能只挂一个名词短语。', ex: 'First and foremost, exercise strengthens our bodies.', exZh: '首先也是最重要的，运动能强健我们的身体。' },
  { id: 'p196', group: 'cohesion', en: 'What is more, ...', zh: '更重要的是……', note: '递进引出第二条理由；正式作文写完整的 What is more，比缩写 What’s more 更稳妥。', ex: 'What is more, team sports teach us how to cooperate.', exZh: '更重要的是，团队运动教会我们如何合作。' },
  { id: 'p197', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Beyond that, ...', zh: '除此之外，……', note: '第三层理由用它，避免与 in addition 反复撞车；that 指代上文，所以前面必须已有论述对象。', ex: 'Beyond that, volunteering helps us value what we have.', exZh: '除此之外，做志愿者让我们更珍惜自己拥有的。' },
  { id: 'p198', group: 'cohesion', en: 'More importantly, ...', zh: '更为关键的是……', note: '把最强的一条理由放在它后面，形成递进高潮；一段里最多用一次，用多了就失去强调效果。', ex: 'More importantly, the experience taught me to stay calm.', exZh: '更为关键的是，这段经历教会我保持冷静。' },
  { id: 'p199', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Not only should we ..., but we can also ...', zh: '我们不仅应该……，而且还能……', note: 'Not only 置于句首必须部分倒装（should 提到主语前），but 后接正常语序；漏掉倒装是高考高频扣分点。', ex: 'Not only should we finish the task, but we can also improve on it.', exZh: '我们不仅应该完成任务，还能在此基础上做得更好。' },
  { id: 'p200', group: 'cohesion', en: 'A case in point is ...', zh: '一个恰当的例子是……', note: '举例段首句，把抽象理由落到具体事例上；is 后接名词或名词短语，不能直接接一个完整句子。', ex: 'A case in point is our class reading corner, which is always full.', exZh: '一个恰当的例子是我们班的图书角，那里总是坐满了人。' },
  { id: 'p201', group: 'cohesion', en: 'To illustrate, ...', zh: '举例来说，……', note: '比 for example 更正式，逗号后接完整句子；不定式后只能接动词原形，别写成 To illustration。', ex: 'To illustrate, many students now review lessons with short videos.', exZh: '举例来说，现在很多学生用短视频复习功课。' },
  { id: 'p202', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Take ... for example.', zh: '以……为例。', note: '祈使句开启具体事例，for example 是固定搭配而非 such as；take 后必须接宾语，事例后面再展开一句。', ex: 'Take my deskmate for example: she failed twice and still kept going.', exZh: '以我同桌为例：她失败了两次，却依然坚持。' },
  { id: 'p203', group: 'cohesion', en: '..., as is often the case in our daily life.', zh: '……，这在我们的日常生活中很常见。', note: 'as 引导非限制性定语从句，指代前面整件事，逗号不可省；此处不能用 which 替换 as。', ex: 'We check our phones constantly, as is often the case in our daily life.', exZh: '我们不停地查看手机，这在日常生活中很常见。' },
  { id: 'p204', group: 'cohesion', en: 'By contrast, ...', zh: '相比之下，……', note: '两种做法形成对照时放段首，介词 by 不可换成 with；前面一句必须先给出被比较的对象。', ex: 'Online learning saves time. By contrast, classroom study offers more discussion.', exZh: '线上学习节省时间。相比之下，课堂学习有更多讨论。' },
  { id: 'p205', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Conversely, ...', zh: '相反，……', note: '用于逻辑上的完全反向，比 on the contrary 更书面；前一句必须是相反情形，否则逻辑断裂。', ex: 'Too much pressure lowers performance. Conversely, a relaxed mind works better.', exZh: '压力过大会拉低表现。相反，放松的头脑效率更高。' },
  { id: 'p206', group: 'cohesion', en: 'On the one hand, ...; on the other hand, ...', zh: '一方面……；另一方面……', note: '两面论证的成对框架，两个分句之间用分号或句号，用逗号连接就是逗号粘连。', ex: 'On the one hand, games relax us; on the other hand, they eat up our time.', exZh: '一方面游戏让我们放松；另一方面它们吞噬我们的时间。' },
  { id: 'p207', group: 'cohesion', en: 'On the contrary, ...', zh: '恰恰相反，……', note: '只在否定前一句后给出相反事实时使用，不能当作 on the other hand 表并列，这是最常见的误用。', ex: 'I am not tired. On the contrary, I feel full of energy.', exZh: '我并不累。恰恰相反，我精力充沛。' },
  { id: 'p208', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Unlike ..., ...', zh: '与……不同的是，……', note: '对比两个人或两件事的开头，介词 unlike 后接名词或 V-ing；逗号后主句不能漏掉自己的主语。', ex: 'Unlike her sister, she prefers reading to chatting.', exZh: '与她姐姐不同，她更喜欢阅读而不是聊天。' },
  { id: 'p209', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Admittedly, ...', zh: '诚然，……', note: '让步句开头，先承认对方有道理，紧接着用 but 或 however 转折；只让步不转折会被判立场不清。', ex: 'Admittedly, the app is convenient. However, it costs us too much time.', exZh: '诚然，这个软件很方便。然而它占用了我们太多时间。' },
  { id: 'p210', group: 'cohesion', en: 'While there is some truth in this view, ...', zh: '尽管这种看法有一定道理，……', note: '放第二段开头做让步，while 从句后必须接主句且逗号不能少；比 although 更书面、更留余地。', ex: 'While there is some truth in this view, it is not the whole story.', exZh: '尽管这种看法有一定道理，但它并非事情的全貌。' },
  { id: 'p211', group: 'cohesion', en: 'There is no denying that ..., yet ...', zh: '不可否认……，然而……', note: '先客观承认再转折，比一味否定更有说服力；that 后接完整句子，yet 是连词，前面用逗号即可。', ex: 'There is no denying that AI helps us study, yet it cannot think for us.', exZh: '不可否认人工智能有助于学习，但它无法替我们思考。' },
  { id: 'p212', group: 'cohesion', en: '... largely accounts for ...', zh: '……在很大程度上解释了……', note: 'account for 表“解释原因”，主语是原因、宾语是结果，顺序写反就成了病句；largely 可换成 partly。', ex: 'Lack of sleep largely accounts for his poor performance.', exZh: '睡眠不足在很大程度上解释了他糟糕的表现。' },
  { id: 'p213', group: 'cohesion', en: '... results in ...', zh: '……导致……', note: 'result in 后接结果，主语是原因；想表达“由……造成”要改用 result from，两者混用是典型错误。', ex: 'Careless habits result in avoidable mistakes.', exZh: '粗心的习惯会导致本可避免的错误。' },
  { id: 'p214', group: 'cohesion', en: '... results from ...', zh: '……源于……', note: 'result from 后接原因，主语是结果；分析成因段用它，比 because of 引导的碎片句更完整。', ex: 'Most of the trouble results from poor time management.', exZh: '大部分麻烦源于时间管理不善。' },
  { id: 'p215', group: 'cohesion', en: '..., thereby improving ...', zh: '……，从而提升了……', note: 'thereby 是副词，后面接 V-ing 而不是 to do；前面的逗号或分号不可省，它无法单靠逗号连两个句子。', ex: 'She kept a diary every day, thereby improving her writing.', exZh: '她每天写日记，从而提高了写作水平。' },
  { id: 'p216', group: 'cohesion', en: '..., which leads to ...', zh: '……，这导致了……', note: 'which 指代前面整句话，逗号不可省；to 是介词，后接名词或 V-ing，不能接动词原形。', ex: 'Students discuss before they write, which leads to better ideas.', exZh: '学生先讨论再动笔，这带来了更好的思路。' },
  { id: 'p217', group: 'cohesion', en: '..., which, however, does not mean that ...', zh: '……，然而这并不意味着……', note: 'however 作插入语被两个逗号夹住，既能转折又不会造成逗号粘连，适合结尾段收紧结论。', ex: 'Technology saves time, which, however, does not mean that we can stop thinking.', exZh: '科技节省了时间，然而这并不意味着我们可以停止思考。' },
  { id: 'p218', group: 'cohesion', en: 'A possible explanation for this is that ...', zh: '对此一个可能的解释是……', note: '分析原因时语气留有余地，比绝对化的 because 更成熟；is 后的 that 引导表语从句，不能省略。', ex: 'A possible explanation for this is that we judge success too quickly.', exZh: '对此一个可能的解释是我们评判成功过于急躁。' },
  { id: 'p219', group: 'cohesion', en: 'However, ...', zh: '然而，……', note: 'however 是副词，不能只靠逗号连接两个句子：要么另起一句，要么用分号……; however, ……。逗号粘连是高考典型扣分点。', ex: 'Many students stay up late. However, this does not improve their grades.', exZh: '许多学生熬夜。然而这并不能提高他们的成绩。' },
  { id: 'p220', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Therefore, ...', zh: '因此，……', note: '和 however 一样是副词，前面要用句号或分号；写成 I was ill, therefore I stayed home 就是逗号粘连。', ex: 'The river has been polluted. Therefore, we must act now.', exZh: '这条河已被污染。因此我们必须立即行动。' },
  { id: 'p221', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Meanwhile, ...', zh: '与此同时，……', note: 'meanwhile 表时间并行而非转折，转折要用 however；它同样是副词，不能仅用逗号连接两个句子。', ex: 'He practised hard. Meanwhile, his teammates were improving quickly.', exZh: '他刻苦训练。与此同时，队友们也在迅速进步。' },
  { id: 'p222', group: 'cohesion', en: 'In the final analysis, ...', zh: '归根结底，……', note: '结尾段第一句，把全文收束到核心判断；一篇文章只用一次，后面若再罗列新例子就失去总结力。', ex: 'In the final analysis, habits rather than talent decide results.', exZh: '归根结底，决定结果的是习惯而非天赋。' },
  { id: 'p223', group: 'cohesion', en: 'It is reasonable to conclude that ...', zh: '综上所述，……是合理的结论', note: '结尾段的客观结论句式，比 I think we can know 正式得多；it 是形式主语，that 不可省。', ex: 'It is reasonable to conclude that the second plan is safer.', exZh: '综上所述，第二个方案更稳妥这一结论是合理的。' },
  { id: 'p224', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Taking everything into consideration, ...', zh: '综合考虑，……', note: '分词短语作全文总结，其逻辑主语必须与主句主语一致，否则构成悬垂结构；短语后加逗号。', ex: 'Taking everything into consideration, we prefer to hold the event on campus.', exZh: '综合考虑，我们更倾向于在校内举办这次活动。' },
  { id: 'p225', group: 'cohesion', en: 'Only in this way can we ...', zh: '只有这样，我们才能……', note: 'Only + 状语置于句首必须部分倒装（can we 提前），漏掉倒装是高频扣分点；结尾用它提建议更有力度。', ex: 'Only in this way can we finish the project on time.', exZh: '只有这样，我们才能按时完成这个项目。' },

  { id: 'p226', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'limit our screen time', zh: '控制屏幕使用时间', note: '科技类建议段的现成动宾搭配，limit 后直接接名词；可放进 we should 或 it is high time we 句型里提建议。', ex: 'We should limit our screen time after school.', exZh: '放学后我们应该控制屏幕使用时间。' },
  { id: 'p227', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'face-to-face interaction', zh: '面对面的交流', note: '写网络利弊的名词化表达，作主语时谓语用单数；比 talk with each other 更具书面感。', ex: 'Face-to-face interaction keeps friendships warm.', exZh: '面对面的交流让友谊保持温度。' },
  { id: 'p228', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'do harm to our concentration', zh: '损害我们的专注力', note: 'harm 前不加冠词，介词用 to 而非 of；主语通常是某种现象，同类结构是 do good to。', ex: 'Constant notifications do harm to our concentration.', exZh: '不断弹出的消息会损害我们的专注力。' },
  { id: 'p229', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'have easy access to information', zh: '便捷地获取信息', note: 'access 必与 to 搭配且前面常带形容词，写成 access to get information 是中式英语。', ex: 'Students now have easy access to information.', exZh: '学生如今能便捷地获取信息。' },
  { id: 'p230', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'a double-edged sword', zh: '一把双刃剑', note: '利弊类话题的总结名词，用 It is a double-edged sword 引出两面分析；这个词已被用滥，一篇作文一次就够。', ex: 'Social media is a double-edged sword in our study.', exZh: '社交媒体在我们的学习中是一把双刃剑。' },
  { id: 'p231', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'raise environmental awareness', zh: '提高环保意识', note: '倡议书结尾号召段的标配，动词用 raise 而不是 rise；后接 among students 可扩大适用范围。', ex: 'The speech aims to raise environmental awareness among students.', exZh: '这次演讲旨在提升学生的环保意识。' },
  { id: 'p232', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'live a low-carbon lifestyle', zh: '践行低碳生活', note: 'live a … lifestyle 是同源宾语结构，冠词 a 不能丢；也可换成 lead a green life 避免重复。', ex: 'More families choose to live a low-carbon lifestyle.', exZh: '越来越多的家庭选择过低碳生活。' },
  { id: 'p233', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'It is our duty to protect the environment.', zh: '保护环境是我们的责任。', note: 'it 作形式主语，真正主语是不定式，放结尾段升华主题；写成 To protect the environment is our duty 会显得生硬。', ex: 'It is our duty to protect the environment for future generations.', exZh: '为子孙后代保护环境是我们的责任。' },
  { id: 'p234', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'cut down on single-use plastic', zh: '减少一次性塑料的使用', note: '措施段的具体动作，介词 on 不能省；比泛泛的 reduce 更具体，single-use 是现成定语。', ex: 'Our school canteen is cutting down on single-use plastic.', exZh: '我们学校的食堂正在减少使用一次性塑料。' },
  { id: 'p235', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'clean and renewable energy', zh: '清洁的可再生能源', note: '写解决方案的名词短语，常与 develop、promote 搭配，别用 raise；renewable 的反义是 non-renewable。', ex: 'Many cities are turning to clean and renewable energy.', exZh: '许多城市正在转向清洁的可再生能源。' },
  { id: 'p236', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'broaden my horizons', zh: '开阔我的眼界', note: '活动收获段几乎万能，但 horizons 必须用复数；一段只用一次，连用会显得内容空洞。', ex: 'Exchange programmes broaden my horizons.', exZh: '交流项目开阔了我的眼界。' },
  { id: 'p237', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'build up my confidence', zh: '建立起自信', note: '写成长变化的高频搭配，build up 后接抽象名词；confidence 不可数，前面不加 a，也不变复数。', ex: 'Small successes gradually build up my confidence.', exZh: '小小的成功逐步建立起我的自信。' },
  { id: 'p238', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'strike a balance between study and rest', zh: '在学习与休息之间取得平衡', note: 'strike 或 keep a balance 后必接 between A and B，且 A、B 词性要一致；写成 between … to 是常见错误。', ex: 'Teenagers should strike a balance between study and rest.', exZh: '青少年应在学习与休息之间取得平衡。' },
  { id: 'p239', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'make the most of every chance', zh: '充分利用每一次机会', note: '建议段用来替代 use，语气更主动；of 后接名词或 V-ing，不能接句子。', ex: 'We should make the most of every chance to speak English.', exZh: '我们应充分利用每一次说英语的机会。' },
  { id: 'p240', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'practise speaking on a regular basis', zh: '定期练习口语', note: 'on a regular basis 比 usually 正式；动词拼 practise、名词拼 practice，混写是扣分点。', ex: 'He practises speaking on a regular basis.', exZh: '他定期练习口语。' },
  { id: 'p241', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'turn a failure into a lesson', zh: '把失败变成一课', note: '成长类结尾的升华语块，turn A into B 两端都可替换；比 learn from failure 更有画面感。', ex: 'With the right attitude, we can turn a failure into a lesson.', exZh: '态度对了，我们就能把失败变成一课。' },
  { id: 'p242', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'carry forward traditional culture', zh: '弘扬传统文化', note: '文化话题的标配搭配，carry forward 表“发扬”，比 develop 更贴切；前面常加 our 或 Chinese 限定。', ex: 'Young people can carry forward traditional culture through everyday actions.', exZh: '年轻人可以通过日常行动弘扬传统文化。' },
  { id: 'p243', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'protect our cultural heritage', zh: '保护我们的文化遗产', note: '介绍古迹、非遗的核心名词，heritage 不可数、不加 s；常与 protect、pass down 搭配。', ex: 'The old town is a treasure we must protect as part of our cultural heritage.', exZh: '这座古镇是我们必须作为文化遗产加以保护的瑰宝。' },
  { id: 'p244', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'gain a better understanding of ...', zh: '对……有更深的了解', note: '写收获时替换 learn about；understanding 前的 a 不能省，介词固定用 of。', ex: 'The visit gave us a better understanding of paper-cutting.', exZh: '这次参观让我们对剪纸有了更深的了解。' },
  { id: 'p245', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'serve as a symbol of ...', zh: '作为……的象征', note: '介绍节日、器物的较高级动词搭配，主语是物；as 不能漏，symbol 后的介词固定用 of。', ex: 'The lantern serves as a symbol of reunion.', exZh: '灯笼是团圆的象征。' },
  { id: 'p246', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'make traditional culture come alive', zh: '让传统文化焕发活力', note: '结尾倡议句好用，make 后的 come alive 是不带 to 的不定式；不能写成 make it living。', ex: 'Short videos can make traditional culture come alive.', exZh: '短视频能让传统文化焕发活力。' },
  { id: 'p247', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'keep fit and stay in good shape', zh: '保持健康与良好体态', note: '写运动好处的并列动词短语，keep fit 比 keep healthy 更地道；fit 已是形容词，后面不要再加 healthy。', ex: 'Swimming helps many teenagers keep fit and stay in good shape.', exZh: '游泳帮助许多青少年保持健康和良好体态。' },
  { id: 'p248', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'relieve the pressure of exams', zh: '缓解考试压力', note: '解压类话题的动宾搭配，relieve 后直接接 pressure，不加介词 from；主语一般是某项活动。', ex: 'Running in the morning helps me relieve the pressure of exams.', exZh: '晨跑帮我缓解考试压力。' },
  { id: 'p249', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'a well-balanced diet', zh: '均衡的饮食', note: '健康话题的名词短语，well-balanced 带连字符；作主语时谓语看 diet，用单数。', ex: 'A well-balanced diet keeps us energetic all day.', exZh: '均衡的饮食让我们全天精力充沛。' },
  { id: 'p250', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'work up a sweat', zh: '出一身汗', note: '描述运动过程的生动短语，比 do exercise 更有画面；sweat 在此为可数用法，须带 a。', ex: 'An hour of badminton is enough to work up a sweat.', exZh: '打一小时羽毛球就足以让我出一身汗。' },
  { id: 'p251', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'regular exercise does wonders for ...', zh: '规律运动对……大有裨益', note: 'do wonders for 表“效果极好”，比 is good for 高一档；主语是单数概念，谓语用 does。', ex: 'Regular exercise does wonders for our mood.', exZh: '规律运动对我们的情绪大有裨益。' },
  { id: 'p252', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'develop a sense of responsibility', zh: '培养责任感', note: '活动意义段的万能搭配；a sense of 后接抽象名词，如 belonging、humour，冠词 a 不可省。', ex: 'Class jobs help students develop a sense of responsibility.', exZh: '班级事务帮助学生培养责任感。' },
  { id: 'p253', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'get along well with my classmates', zh: '与同学相处融洽', note: 'well 放在 with 前更自然；主语是第三人称单数时才写 gets along，别和复数主语混用。', ex: 'I get along well with my classmates.', exZh: '我和同学们相处融洽。' },
  { id: 'p254', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'offer a helping hand to others', zh: '向他人伸出援手', note: '写助人情节的现成语块，比 help others 生动；to 后接人，不能接动词原形。', ex: 'She always offers a helping hand to others.', exZh: '她总是向别人伸出援手。' },
  { id: 'p255', group: 'topicchunks', en: "put ourselves in others' shoes", zh: '设身处地为他人着想', note: '写同理心、沟通话题的地道说法，shoes 用复数；反身代词要与主语一致，we 配 ourselves。', ex: "Communication begins when we put ourselves in others' shoes.", exZh: '当我们设身处地为他人着想时，沟通才真正开始。' },
  { id: 'p256', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'make a positive contribution to society', zh: '为社会做出积极贡献', note: '结尾升华常用，contribution 可数需带 a；to 后接名词或 V-ing，不能接动词原形。', ex: 'Volunteering lets students make a positive contribution to society.', exZh: '志愿服务让学生能为社会做出积极贡献。' },
  { id: 'p257', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'Persistence pays off.', zh: '坚持终有回报。', note: '可作点题句或结尾金句；主语 persistence 不可数，谓语用单数 pays off，别写成 are paid off。', ex: 'The project taught me that persistence pays off.', exZh: '这个项目让我明白坚持终有回报。' },
  { id: 'p258', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'a sense of achievement', zh: '成就感', note: '描写活动收获的现成名词，常配 give me 或 fill me with；achievement 表抽象含义时不加冠词。', ex: 'Finishing the race gave me a real sense of achievement.', exZh: '跑完比赛给了我真正的成就感。' },
  { id: 'p259', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'rise to the challenge', zh: '迎接（并成功应对）挑战', note: '写克服困难的动词搭配，rise to 比 face 多了“应对成功”的含义；讲述过去经历要用 rose to。', ex: 'She rose to the challenge and led the team to victory.', exZh: '她勇敢迎接挑战，带领队伍取得胜利。' },
  { id: 'p260', group: 'topicchunks', en: 'It was tough, but it was worth it.', zh: '虽然艰难，但很值得。', note: '记叙文、读后续写结尾的情感升华句；worth 后已隐含宾语，不能再写成 worth to do it。', ex: 'Training took the whole summer; it was tough, but it was worth it.', exZh: '训练耗掉了整个暑假；虽然艰难，但很值得。' },
